{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And you grumbled.</b> Lashon ha-ra, evil speech; and likewise ״דִּבְרֵי נִרְגָּן״ (Proverbs 18) — a person who utters slander." "<b>In YHWH's hatred of us.</b> Yet it was He who loved you — but you hate Him. A parable of a commoner: what is in your heart against your friend is what is in his heart against you (Sifrei)." "<b>In YHWH's hatred of us He brought us out of the land of Egypt.</b> His bringing us out was for hatred. A parable of a king of flesh and blood who had two sons and had two fields — one irrigated and one rain-fed. To the one he loves he gives the irrigated one; to the one he hates he gives the rain-fed one. The land of Egypt is irrigated, for the Nile rises and waters it, and the land of Canaan is rain-fed — and He brought us out of Egypt to give us the land of Canaan (Bereshit Rabbah 17)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:33.717584421Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}